nt for bulgaria's  next generation eu plan for your prime  minister thank you so much  thank you  thank you so much  indeed on these two topics the plan is  really good  um if you it's one of the most green  plants that we have uh in the european  union and i think it's now the 23rd plan  that  um the commission is approving  with 60  of the plan going into the european  green deal with all the topics i've just  been  describing  so very important is you have a  trajectory to cut greenhouse gas  emissions  by 40 percent by 2025 this is very  ambitious but it's also very necessary  so congratulations on that  you triple power generation from  renewables by 2026  and  you have a phase phase-out coal-powered  plants by 2038 so there's a real  structure real plan behind it  to cut emissions on one hand and on the  other hand to invest heavily into  renewables and of course the storage  capacities the battery capacities that  are so important i was mentioning also  the interconnections that in my view are  very important because you have to  diversify  the possibility to have access for  example to pipeline gas a very important  topic so it's one of the most ambitious  plans we have  what the european green deal is  concerned  the second part of your questions is  indeed you address  two of the  main major topics that are necessary in  the cvm for example this is a big step  forward  there's the reform of the  anti-corruption commission  is one big pillar that is important and  the other important pillar is the  accountability of the prosecutor general  so two big required reform steps within  the cvm so a big step forward also to  achieve your goals  [Music]  [Music]  so there's a very clear plan and goals  described in the rrp what this topic is  concerned  um the the main overarching headline  here is accountability  and this is in every system important  that there are checks and balances  with power  accountability has to go hand in hand  these are the reform steps 